          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: धूर्तः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धूर्तः — dhūrtaḥ — \"a rogue; a cheat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सः नरः धूर्तः अस्ति। saḥ naraḥ dhūrtaḥ asti. That man is a rogue."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धूर्तः (dhūrtaḥ) comes from the root √dhūrv, \"to hurt\" (MW also names √dhvṛ); MW gives dhūrta as cunning and, as a noun, a rogue or swindler (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
